.TH BEDIT 1 "2026-08-14" "bedit 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bedit \- review tracked file history, revisions, search results, and restore points
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bedit
.BI -r " FILE [REV]"
.br
.B bedit
.BI -g " FILE [REV]"
.br
.B bedit
.BI -s " TERM"
.br
.B bedit
.BI -s " FILE TERM"
.br
.B bedit
.BI -w " FILE"
.br
.B bedit
.BI -d " FILE REV1 REV2"
.br
.B bedit
.BI -h " [FILE]"
.br
.B bedit
.BI -ls " [.|DIR|FILE|*]"
.br
.B bedit
.B --version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bedit
opens the interactive terminal history UI when run bare on a terminal, and reads
or mutates the tracked revision store when invoked with explicit CLI options.
.PP
Command ownership:
.TP
.B --version, -V
Print the installed Bedit version without opening the repository or TUI.
.TP
.B -r, -restore FILE [REV]
Restore FILE to REV. If REV is omitted, restores the latest stored revision.
.TP
.B -g, -get FILE [REV]
Print a stored revision to stdout. If REV is omitted, prints the latest stored revision.
.TP
.B -s, -search TERM
Search all tracked revisions of all tracked files.
.TP
.B -s, -search FILE TERM
Search all tracked revisions of FILE.
.TP
.B -w, -where FILE
Show tracked paths for FILE.
.TP
.B -d, -diff FILE REV1 REV2
Diff two stored revisions.
.TP
.B -h, -history [FILE]
Show history for all tracked files, or only FILE when given.
.TP
.B -ls [.|DIR|FILE|*]
List stored history artifacts in the selected scope. The default scope is the
current directory; DIR selects files directly in that directory, FILE selects
one tracked file, and * selects all tracked paths. Output columns are
.B FILE  REV  TYPE  WHEN  EDIT  USER,
where TYPE identifies access metadata, a backup payload, or a diff; EDIT is the
recorded editor and USER is the recorded actor. Rows are newest first by default.
.SH SEARCH OUTPUT
Search output is grouped by file and revision.
.PP
.nf
FILE: /root/a.txt
  rev 1:
    1: one
  rev 2:
    1: one
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/bedit/access
access records
.TP
.I ~/bedit/backups
stored revision payloads
.TP
.I ~/bedit/edits
stored diffs
.TP
.I ~/bedit/dirs
directory metadata and links
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bvi (1),
.BR bnvim (1),
.BR bed (1),
.BR bnano (1),
.BR bemacs (1),
.BR bpico (1)
